    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d427-a1">

                <pb facs="0456" n="450" xml:id="pg450"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Inclosure in No. 242.—Translation.]</seg></opener>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Moret to Mr. Taylor</hi>.</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><hi rendition="#small-caps">Ministry of
                            State</hi>, <lb/>
                        <placeName type="venue"><hi rendition="#italic">Palace</hi></placeName>,
                            <date calendar="gregorian" when="1894-10-01"><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >October 1, 1894</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p rendition="#flush"><hi rendition="#small-caps">Excellency.</hi></p>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">My Dear Sir</hi>: While acknowledging the receipt of
                    your note of the 29th, I hasten to inform you that the delay in answering the
                    communication which you had the kindness to address to me on the 22d of June
                    last resulted from the fact that I have been heretofore unable, for well-known
                    reasons, to communicate its contents to the council of ministers.</p>
                <p>I have already had occasion to inform your excellency that the nature of this
                    affair, on account of the parlimentary state in which it now is, makes it
                    impossible for the ministry of state alone to adopt any decision in the matter
                    without the concurrence of the council of ministers.</p>
                <p>As soon as the ministers meet again in Madrid, and the president is present at
                    the sessions, I will consult with him on the subject.</p>
                <p>I seize, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">S. Moret.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
